clearcote: schema-2 draws from measured shares; navigator.connection served from the persona.

Shares come from the decontaminated audit corpus, Windows desktop Chromium, n = 208 (LOCAL-ONLY
file 72): 26 desktops with a touchscreen (24 of them 10 points; every one keeps a fine primary
pointer with any-pointer:coarse), 13 with a P3 gamut, rtt 50 ms in 82 of 180 reporting captures
(100 ms in 47, 0 in 15), downlink 10 Mbps in 112 of 180 with a real 1.25..1.75 Mbps cluster,
and an AudioContext sampleRate of 44100 in 207 of 208. Schema 2 draws touch, gamut, rtt and
downlink from those counts on Chrome's own grids (50 ms multiples <= 3 s; 50 kbps buckets
<= 10 Mbps) and serves 44100 Hz. Schema 1 is unchanged: the new persona fields default to the
constants 150 hard-coded (50 ms / 10 Mbps) and its sample rate stays 48000. The validator
rejects any connection value off the grid in every schema.

